\end{align}
$$

Step 1: Write down the correct formula for the area of a triangle.

$$
A  = \frac{b \times h}{2}
$$

Step 2: Substitute the correct values into the formula.

$$
\begin{align}
 A  &= \frac{b \times h}{2}\\
 A  &= \frac{12  \times 5 }{2}
\end{align}
$$

Step 3: Do the calculation and remember to show the correct units in your answer.

$$
\begin{align}
 A  &= \frac{b \times h}{2} \\
 A  &= \frac{12 \times 5 }{2}\\
 A  &= \frac{60 }{2}\\
 A  &= 30 \text{ cm$^{2}$}
\end{align}
$$

